e to the team i mean a  four-year 87 million dollar deal uh that  is pretty nice of a guy and hey i i feel  like he's been disrespected at times in  seattle i feel like he gets disrespected  nationally at times he is without  question one of the three or four best  quarterbacks in football the last two or  three years and for some reason i feel  like when you talk to joe you know joe  football fan he doesn't always get put  in that conversation and i don't know if  that's because people think he's cheesy  or a dork in some way but i know on the  football field he's awesome and that's  all there is to it  his new money average at the time he did  the deal was 21.9 million just behind  aaron rodgers who was at 22. and the  problem is we saw guys like  andrew luck derek carr matthew stafford  kirk cousins matt ryan and aaron rodgers  again all out to the point where right  yeah eli manning's making in the same  ballpark but there's a lot of guys  making more who aren't anywhere close to  russell wilson and i think that's why  there's frustration and and one of these  true franchise quarterbacks chris is  going to say  well kirk cousins he's not one of the  top five guys and look at what he was  able to do we're going to do that too  and with the rules that protect  quarterbacks more than ever before and i  know the alex smith injury happened last  year that's a fluke quarterbacks are  protected more than ever before you can  get away with carrying the injury risk  and as long as wilson is able to say no  to the seahawks  and when they put those big numbers on  the table that are big but not as big as  they could be he can force his way to  the open market now that doesn't mean  the giants want him i don't know that  the giants want him i don't know that  the giants would pay him my point is  that russell wilson if he wants to can  ultimately end up on the open market  with years left in his prime and god  knows how much he would get if he would  be available to anyone 